    "body": "## Summary\n- add a requester-only acceptance-funding preflight for proposal jobs\n- derive the real positive escrow delta from the held transaction and current wallet contribution\n- reuse the existing Stripe wallet top-up/payment ledger instead of creating proposal-specific payment state\n- retry authoritative proposal acceptance only after the signed Stripe webhook makes funds visible in the wallet\n- keep stale/withdrawn/blocked proposal races safe: payment may finish as wallet credit, but the webhook never assigns a worker\n- handle the existing 1.00 PLN online-payment minimum and 10,000.00 PLN single-top-up maximum explicitly\n- add runtime PostgreSQL smoke coverage for privacy, read-only quoting, insufficient-funds rollback and exact escrow-delta locking\n- document funding, concurrency, ledger and privacy semantics\n\n## Ledger / security invariants\n- funding preflight never mutates wallet or escrow\n- only the requester can read a funding quote\n- proposal competitors do not gain wallet/payment visibility\n- `POST .../accept` remains the authoritative lock/revalidation point\n- Stripe success credits the existing wallet ledger exactly as a normal top-up; it cannot accept stale marketplace state\n- escrow adjustment remains idempotently keyed by job + proposal\n\n## Validation\nCI is expected to run Maven verify, web audit/lint/build, container runtime smoke, and the new negotiated proposal acceptance funding smoke on the latest PR head.",
